{
  "loaded": [
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::whoami",
      "description": "Your address, role, budget, direct reports, open tasks, outstanding delegations and charter.",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::inbox",
      "description": "The messages for this run. For root (the human) this lists unread messages and marks them read.",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::delegate",
      "description": "Assign a task to one of your direct reports.\n\nto: the report's address (e.g. \"ceo/cto\"). title: a few words. goal: what outcome is needed and why.\nacceptance: concrete, checkable criteria for \"done\". inputs: paths (relative to the org root) the\nreport should read. budget: runs handed to the report from your own budget. If you omit it, the default is\nmin(default_budget from ORG.md, your budget - reserve), where the reserve keeps one run per outstanding\ndelegation plus one for this one; if that is below 1 the call fails and tells you your options.\nAn explicit budget must leave that same reserve.\nCopy the relevant acceptance criteria verbatim from the task you are working on; never paraphrase or relax them.\nrevises: when sending work back for rework, the id of the earlier task you sent to the same report.\nReturns the task id. Do not wait for the result: end your run, the result will wake you.\n",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "to": {
            "title": "To",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": {
            "title": "Title",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "goal": {
            "title": "Goal",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "acceptance": {
            "title": "Acceptance",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "inputs": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Inputs"
          },
          "budget": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Budget"
          },
          "revises": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Revises"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "to",
          "title",
          "goal",
          "acceptance"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::report",
      "description": "Answer a task assigned to you. Goes to whoever assigned it.\n\nstatus: \"done\" (every acceptance criterion verifiably met), \"failed\", or \"blocked\" (say what would unblock it).\n`done` and `failed` are final: a second report is refused. `blocked` is not: once the blocker is resolved\nyou may report the task again, once per blocked report (any status; the new report supersedes the old one),\nunder the same rules. A `send` note never changes a task's outcome and must not claim criteria are met.\nsummary: at most ~10 lines; this is all your manager reads by default. artifacts: paths of the\nfiles that hold the work; they must exist. Files in the organization: path relative to the org root.\nFiles in your workspace: the ABSOLUTE path (anything else outside the organization is refused). The runtime\nannotates each with its word count and whether it changed since the task was assigned.\nlessons: required when the task is a request for a service, whatever the status - done, failed or blocked\n(1-3 lines, at most 800 characters: what worked or went wrong, what to change in the playbook, the evidence:\nruns, rework, review findings); it is recorded in the result and reviewed before the next request. Optional\notherwise.\n",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "task_id": {
            "title": "Task Id",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "status": {
            "title": "Status",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "summary": {
            "title": "Summary",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "artifacts": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Artifacts"
          },
          "lessons": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Lessons"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "task_id",
          "status",
          "summary"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::send",
      "description": "Send a note: a question, information, or an escalation.\n\nAllowed recipients: your parent, your direct reports, your siblings, or the sender of the message\nyou reply to (set reply_to to its id). budget: runs to move along with the note (optional): extra runs\ngranted to a direct report, or unneeded runs given back to your PARENT (never to a sibling). Runs you\nhave left return to your parent by themselves with your final `done`/`failed` report when nothing else\nis open for you; use this only to give some back earlier. To pull unspent runs BACK from an idle direct\nreport instead (budget stranded in a team that cannot use it), use `reclaim`.\n",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "to": {
            "title": "To",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "body": {
            "title": "Body",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": {
            "default": "",
            "title": "Title",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "reply_to": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Reply To"
          },
          "budget": {
            "default": 0,
            "title": "Budget",
            "type": "integer"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "to",
          "body"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::reclaim",
      "description": "Pull unspent budget back from one of your DIRECT reports (a manager from its team; root from its top agents).\n\nreport: its short name or address. budget: how many runs (default: all it has left). Only an idle report:\nno open task, nothing delegated and outstanding, not running, no unread mail that would wake it; otherwise the\ncall is refused and says why. Not from deeper down (a manager reclaims from its own reports). The report is\nnot woken and gets no message; you get the runs (they join your budget at once, and then a delegation or\n`send(..., budget=N)` can move them to whoever needs them). Use it before asking your parent for more runs\nwhile a sibling team sits on unspent ones.\n",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "report": {
            "title": "Report",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "budget": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Budget"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "report"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::hire",
      "description": "Create a direct report (only if your charter allows hiring).\n\nname: lowercase-dashed (becomes the address <you>/<name>). role: a short job title.\ncharter: markdown with purpose, responsibilities, decision rights, what to escalate, quality bar.\nmodel: kiro model id (optional; unset = the organization's default model, claude-sonnet-5.5). tools: kiro built-in tools to grant, only ones you have yourself\n(e.g. \"read\", \"write\", \"shell\"). can_hire: whether the report may build its own team; only root (the user) or an approved plan can grant it.\nmax_children: the most direct reports it may have (for an agent hiring: at most its own); a report without can_hire gets 0.\nworkspace: directory the report works in (must be inside yours).\ninputs: absolute folders the report may only READ (never change); a manager can give only folders inside its\nown inputs or workspace. A report with `read` and no workspace/inputs reads nothing outside the org.\nA new report has no budget until you delegate a task to it.\n",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "name": {
            "title": "Name",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "role": {
            "title": "Role",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "charter": {
            "title": "Charter",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "model": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Model"
          },
          "tools": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Tools"
          },
          "can_hire": {
            "default": false,
            "title": "Can Hire",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "max_children": {
            "default": 5,
            "title": "Max Children",
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "workspace": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Workspace"
          },
          "inputs": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Inputs"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "name",
          "role",
          "charter"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::retire",
      "description": "Remove a direct report and its team (name: its short name or full address, e.g. \"eng\" or \"ceo/eng\").\n\nTheir open tasks are reported to you as failed, and the team's unspent budget is returned to you.\n",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "name": {
            "title": "Name",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "reason": {
            "title": "Reason",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "name",
          "reason"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::org_read",
      "description": "The ORGANIZATION's read tool (kiro shows it as @hirearchy/org_read; not kiro's built-in `read`, which reads the\n        workspace). kiro's built-in file tools (`read_file`, `list_directory`) read the workspace, inputs and, by absolute path, the organization; this tool is the organization's relative-path reader, called `org_read` for you. Reads a file (with word count and modification time) or lists a directory in the organization. Paths\n        are relative to the org root, e.g. \"ceo/writer/work/brief.md\". Outside the organization only ABSOLUTE paths work,\n        and only inside your workspace, your read-only inputs, or the workspace of an agent in your team (to verify\n        what your reports made); anything else is refused.",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "path": {
            "default": ".",
            "title": "Path",
            "type": "string"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::org_write",
      "description": "Write an ORGANIZATION file (kiro shows this tool as @hirearchy/org_write; it is NOT kiro's built-in `write`, which\n        writes the workspace). kiro's built-in file tools are `fs_write`, `str_replace`, `fs_append` and `delete_file`; this hirearchy tool is called `org_write` for you. Use it for your memory, notes and artifacts inside your own org directory. Paths are\n        relative to the org root, like every path here, so they start with your address: e.g. \"<you>/MEMORY.md\" or\n        \"<you>/work/plan.md\".\n\n        You may also rewrite a direct report's charter (\"<you>/<name>/AGENT.md\"). Inboxes, logs and your own\n        charter are managed by the runtime; use send/delegate/report to communicate. A charter rewrite keeps every\n        frontmatter key (tools, inputs, model, ...) that your new text does not set; the reply lists what was kept\n        and what changed.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "path": {
            "title": "Path",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "content": {
            "title": "Content",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "append": {
            "default": false,
            "title": "Append",
            "type": "boolean"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "path",
          "content"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::status",
      "description": "The whole organization as a tree: each agent's role, state, budget and workload.",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::health",
      "description": "Health report (stuck, expensive, low-quality, wasteful, idle, paused) for an agent and its subtree.\n\nagent: yourself or an agent in your own subtree (root may ask about anyone). Default: your own subtree\n(root: the whole organization). Use it to decide whom to follow up with, rework, re-budget or retire.\n",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "agent": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Agent"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "not_found": [],
  "note": "These tools are now loaded for the rest of this session. To RUN one, call tool_call with { \"tool_id\": \"namespace::tool\", \"arguments\": { ... } } (use the tool_id shown for each result, and arguments matching its input_schema). Do not call tool_load again for tools you have already loaded."
}
